32:## Framework change ledger
36:| `src/framework/passes/define-pass.ts` (`applyPass`, beside `definePass`) | Add `applyNativePassSync(pass, before, verify)` for synchronous native `definePass` kernels with empty analysis needs/preservation and a mandatory synchronous meaning check. It returns a `PassResult` on acceptance. Factor the native candidate construction, structural diff, correspondence and declared-write checks out of the existing runner so both paths use them. | Calling `applyPass` directly returns a Promise, which breaks `optimizeTix`. Copying its structural checks into Tix gives two implementations of pass acceptance. |
39:The sync path takes the same pass declaration and native kernel as the async path. Its supported subset uses neither managed transformation clauses nor effects. The required `verify(before, candidate)` returns the framework's `CheckResult`. A negative verdict rejects the pass and carries its evidence. The tensor driver supplies a verifier built from v6 differential invariants. Each binds two `tensor.indexed@1` artifact ports. The baseline runs at the relation's reference precision and the subject always runs at f32. Use the existing synchronous callback check for its result and the kernel result. The sync path uses private views for the two revisions and the caller takes the accepted artifact. This needs neither a shared `IRStore` head nor a synchronous `AnalysisManager`. The existing passes barrel re-exports `define-pass.ts`.
43:## Source and call domain
45:The surface is the supplied Tix grammar. Programs contain named functions with one or more rank-one-or-higher f32 parameters, zero or more tensor definitions and one named tensor return. Functions can return an input. At a call, every parameter has its declared rank, consistent concrete extents and row-major data of length equal to the product of its extents. Shape bindings and extents are nonnegative integers, including zero. Extents, offsets and allocations must be representable on the host, accesses in bounds and input elements finite. Only the contract's *sample* sizes are small.
53:## Artifact and execution
66:Implement `compileTix`, `runTix` and `optimizeTix` as the specified synchronous exports from `src/tensor/index.ts` (built to `dist/tensor/index.js`). The opaque program holds the compiled origin, current artifact and accepted origin relation, initially exact. This retains the same reference even across repeated optimize calls. `runTix` evaluates the current artifact. Typed buffers live only at execution time. The artifact format accepts finite plain data, normalizes numeric negative zero, and rejects typed arrays. Literal text plus explicit negation preserves source arithmetic without extending the format.
70:## Sampled meaning contract
77:| Values | Per retained shape use all ones, the repeated flat motif `[1,0,0,0,2^-24,2^-24,0,0]`, and signed f32 values from `seededRandom(20)` mapped to `[-1,1)` in parameter/element order. For parameters declared exactly `f32[1]`, use positive scalar values (1, 2⁻¹⁰ and 2⁻⁵ respectively) so the cases vary an explicit layernorm epsilon while keeping its scale valid. The evaluator itself accepts general finite inputs. |
83:## Rewrites and decisive tests
97:For `y[i] = sum(k) x[i,k]`, give one row the eight-element motif above. The measured serial f32 result is `0x3f800000` (1). The blocked result is `0x3f800001` (1 + 2⁻²³), exactly the f64 reference. The *same changed candidate* must fail exact and pass tolerance. A wrong split using only full blocks returns 8 on nine ones. The reference is 9 and the permitted error is 0.0001. Test that it fails tolerance. Assert the structural rewrite and the returned program's execution alongside the verdict so an identity kernel cannot pass as an optimization.
99:## Corpus and verification after review
107:| `layernorm` | Per-row mean and centered variance, explicit `gamma[D]`, `beta[D]`, `eps[1]`. Constant rows give beta, nonconstant rows exercise gamma and epsilon. |
112:Use Node tests in `tests/tensor/` importing the built API. Cover token positions after comments, reduction precedence, two meanings of max, normalized shape equality, inferred/annotated extents, affine-only reduction errors, single assignment, and affine shape binding. Use hand-derived results for row-major reads, empty folds, multi-axis order, signed zero and per-operation rounding (`4097*4097 - 16785408` gives 0 in f32 and 1 in f64). Exercise both orders of passes, repeated optimize calls, rejection followed by another pass, the two mutants, and a second callable function so one agreeing function cannot authorize a bad program.
